1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:18,900
Every family pays for subscriptions
nobody uses. And every parent fears an
AI that orders, or unlocks, without
asking. Hearth is the Alexa Plus agent
that found eight hundred dollars of
waste in our home, and cannot spend one
dollar until you tap once.

2
00:00:18,900 --> 00:00:56,700
Watch. Alexa, ask Hearth to save me 800
dollars. She audits five subscriptions
live. StreamBox dormant sixty-eight
days, Metro Fitness one visit in forty-
five, Cloud Gaming untouched. Three
cards: eight hundred three dollars and
seventy-six cents a year. I stage one.
Nothing is cancelled. I tap Approve.
Sealed receipt. I tap Undo. Money back.
Nothing moved until I tapped. Everything
undoes.

3
00:00:56,700 --> 00:01:21,600
Same contract for groceries. We are out
of everything. Fix groceries. Coffee
empties in two days. Five items, fifteen
percent Subscribe and Save, Prime slot
tomorrow eight to eleven. Still nothing
ordered. One tap approves. One tap
undoes. This maps straight onto Alexa
Plus checkout and Subscribe and Save.

4
00:01:21,600 --> 00:01:35,800
Leo cannot spend or unlock. By design,
not by prompt. And at 3am Hearth does
not scream sensor open. It proves why.
Wind, pressure drop, zero thermal
signatures. Intruder disproved, proof
sealed.

5
00:01:35,800 --> 00:01:59,500
Real Strands Agents SDK. Bedrock
AgentCore memory. Fifty-one MCP tools
over Streamable HTTP. Agent Skills. And
our open-source Strands-to-MCP adapter.
Clone, one script, no keys, no device.
Hearth: Alexa that saves you eight
hundred dollars, and never spends one
without you. Thank you.
